Ah, that makes perfect sense. The issue here is that MUI’s autoSelect prop treats **pressing Tab** and **clicking away** as the exact same action (they both trigger a blur event on the input). If autoSelect is enabled, it forces a selection whenever the field loses focus, no matter how it happened.
To fix this so it **only** selects on Tab and **ignores** clicks elsewhere, we need to:
 1. **Remove** the autoSelect prop entirely.
 2. Add a custom onKeyDown listener to manually catch the Tab key.
 3. Programmatically pick the first available option when Tab is pressed.
Here are the updated blocks for Branch, CGL, and Currency to achieve exactly this UX:
### 1. Branch Update
```jsx
{/* Branch */}
<Grid item size={{ xl: 1.5, lg: 2 }}>
  <Autocomplete
    autoHighlight
    // autoSelect REMOVED to prevent selection on click-away
    popupIcon={null}
    options={
      row.branch && !branchSearch.options.some((o) => o.code === row.branch.code)
        ? [row.branch, ...branchSearch.options]
        : branchSearch.options
    }
    getOptionLabel={(option) => option && option.code ? `${option.code} - ${option.name}` : ""}
    slotProps={{
      popper: {
        placement: 'bottom-start',
        modifiers: [{ name: 'flip', enabled: false }, { name: 'preventOverflow', enabled: false }],
      },
    }}
    value={row.branch || null}
    onChange={(event, newValue) => handleRowChange(row.id, "branch", newValue)}
    inputValue={branchInputValues[row.id] || ""}
    onInputChange={(event, newInputValue, reason) => {
      if (reason === 'input') {
        const cleanInput = newInputValue.replace(BRANCH_REPLACE_REGEX, "").substring(0, 5);
        setBranchInputValues(prev => ({ ...prev, [row.id]: cleanInput }));
        searchBranches(cleanInput, row.id);
      } else {
        setBranchInputValues(prev => ({ ...prev, [row.id]: newInputValue }));
      }
    }}
    // --- ADDED INTERCEPTOR FOR TAB KEY ---
    onKeyDown={(e) => {
      if (e.key === 'Tab' && !row.branch && branchSearch.options?.length > 0) {
        // Automatically set the first suggestion when Tab is pressed
        handleRowChange(row.id, "branch", branchSearch.options[0]);
      }
    }}
    loading={branchSearch.loadingId === row.id} 
    filterOptions={(x) => x}
    isOptionEqualToValue={(option, value) => option?.code === value?.code}
    noOptionsText={(branchInputValues[row.id] || "").length < 3 ? "Please enter at least 3 digits" : "No Branch found"}
    renderInput={(params) => (
      <Tooltip title="Search by Branch Code" placement="top-start">
        <TextField
          {...params}
          label="Branch *"
          placeholder="Enter branch code..."
          InputLabelProps={{ shrink: true }}
          inputProps={{
            ...params.inputProps,
            style: { textOverflow: 'ellipsis', whiteSpace: 'nowrap', overflow: 'hidden' }
          }}
          InputProps={{
            ...params.InputProps,
            endAdornment: (
              <Box>
                {branchSearch.loadingId === row.id ? (<CircularProgress color="inherit" size={20} />) : null}
                {params.InputProps.endAdornment}
              </Box>
            )
          }}
        />
      </Tooltip>
    )}
  />
  <Typography variant="caption" sx={jpStyles.captionText}>
    Min 3 Digits Required Search
  </Typography>
</Grid>

```
